led faced  with stuck out tongue and winking eye  emoji pedia describes this emoji as a  face showing a stuck out tongue winking  at the same time used in an attempt to  be wacky zany or otherwise joking so it  looks like the people who've been using  it jokingly win that's what the emoji  was meant for did you make a mistake and  completely forget something this emoji  is perfect to add on at the end of your  text to describe how goofy it was to  forget now that we know it's real  meaning the emoji works in so many cases  make sure to tell all your friends so  they can make sure they're using it  correctly  - crying laughing well at first glance  the tears in this emoji can cause you to  think that it's sad the emoji is  actually meant to be used in situations  that are so funny it causes you to cry  the emoji is literally crying laughing  officially called tears of joy this  emoji is an all-time favorite  researchers analysed over 70,000 pleats  and came up with a list of the 751 most  used emojis and the top with the tears  of joy emoji so does that mean most  people are so happy that they're crying  most of the  I'm not quite the studies showed that  this correlation has to do with how much  people want to be perceived as happy fun  people this is also the reason why the  top of the list was filled with other  happy emojis people want to seem happy  so they use happy emojis when you think  about it it makes perfect sense often  when we communicate with others we want  to show our happy side and leave out the  negative emojis are a great way to do  that and the crying laughing emoji is  the ultimate happy emoji so next time  you use it just know you're in good  company that's it for the 10 emojis that  don't mean what you think they do do you  know any more emojis with surprised  meanings let us know in the comments and  make sure to share this video with your  friends to save them from making any  texting mistakes bye bye  [Music]

